 "basis": "homes = gas-heated homes = meters x 0.86. Domestic gas meters in GB, calendar year 2024 (DESNZ subnational gas statistics: meters on the domestic consumption profile, Annual Quantity < 73,200 kWh, with a valid reading). This counts gas METERS, not gas-HEATED homes: it includes some cooking-only or vacant connections and misses gas-heated flats on a shared/communal meter or on a non-domestic (>73,200 kWh) meter. Used as the scaling count of homes on the gas grid; see assumptions for the size of the difference.",
 "method": "Each DESNZ MSOA (England & Wales, 2021 MSOAs) and Intermediate Zone (Scotland, 2022) domestic meter count was placed at its published centroid (ONS population-weighted centroids for MSOAs; Scottish Government IZ centroids) and assigned by point-in-polygon to the NESO DNO licence area polygon that contains it; licence areas map one-to-one to the 14 GSP group letters A..P used by Octopus. Centroids outside every polygon (coastal generalisation) go to the nearest polygon. DESNZ's 'Unallocated' meters were spread pro rata. Cross-checked against the DESNZ local-authority file total for the same year. Reproduce with: .venv/bin/python -I scripts/spark/gb_national_scale.py",
 "assumptions": [
  "Small-area assignment is by centroid: an MSOA/IZ whose area straddles a licence-area boundary goes wholly to the area holding its centroid. MSOAs hold ~3,000 meters each, so the error is a boundary effect of order one MSOA per straddle, not a regional bias.",
  "DESNZ 'Unallocated' domestic meters (33,100) were shared pro rata across regions (factor 1.00134).",
  "DNO licence areas (NESO, 2024-05-03) are taken as identical to the GSP groups / Octopus region letters; this is how the letters are defined (A Eastern = UKPN East, ... P = SSEN North of Scotland).",
  "Meters are not homes. A meter count over-states gas-HEATED homes by cooking-only and vacant connections and under-states them by communal-boiler flats; the net effect is not measured here. If a gas-heated-homes basis is needed, the census 2021 (England & Wales) 'mains gas only' central heating share is the usual scaler: see census_2021_ew_cross_check for the ratios (England & Wales only).",
  "Year is the latest in the DESNZ file; meter counts are a snapshot, not the stock of buildings.",
  "Northern Ireland is outside GB and outside the DESNZ GB gas series."
 ],
